      "value": "@{5bbe4a1af3300d438fe24a2c|full_name}: There's a bare minimum for VR in terms of hardware anyways, back when I posted about this I was running a Core i5 3rd gen with a GTX 970, which is ironicly the bare minimum recommended by Oculus on the box. I had no issues. \n\nAlso deferred rendering is actually less of a performance hit as it's more predictable then forward rendering. It's all pretty well documented on Unity's website.",
